window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["34"]={"https://theconversation.com/large-companies-can-still-fall-short-on-their-climate-commitments-heres-what-must-change-295971":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"e40f8661e535c9aa156661cc9abdd3caf6c52402426380ba7a0435f4219f3c6c","read":"https://theconversation.com/large-companies-can-still-fall-short-on-their-climate-commitments-heres-what-must-change-295971","bytes":184001,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Large companies can still fall short on their climate commitments. Here’s what must change","by":[{"n":"Rebekkah Markey-Towler","r":"Postdoctoral research fellow, Monash University"},{"n":"Bei Cui","r":"Senior research fellow, Monash University"},{"n":"Ella Vines","r":"Post-doctoral researcher, Green Lab, Monash University"}],"pub":"2026-11-16T23:58:16Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["International climate conferences like the ",["COP31 climate summit","https://cop.sifiratikvakfi.org/en/"],", now in its second week, tend to focus on the role of individual countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet, more than half of global CO₂ emissions from fossil fuel and cement are produced by just ",["32 companies","https://carbonmajors.org/briefing/Carbon-Majors-2024-Data-Update-35466"],". Many have already set ",["net zero targets","https://ca1-nzt.edcdn.com/PDFs-and-Excels/Net_Zero_Stocktake_2026.pdf?v=1793874786"]," in response to mounting international pressure."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, ",["new research","https://www.monash.edu/business/mcfs/our-research/all-projects/climate-change/decarbonisation-credibility-benchmarking-framework"]," into Australian companies, from the Monash Business School Green Lab, calls the credibility of these targets into question – revealing a major gap between what some companies say and do regarding emissions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Without stronger regulation, large companies will continue to be vague about how they will achieve their climate commitments."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Yes, the COP climate talks are far from perfect. But they still hold the power for change","https://theconversation.com/yes-the-cop-climate-talks-are-far-from-perfect-but-they-still-hold-the-power-for-change-295350"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Australia’s corporate emitters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Our ",["new study","https://www.monash.edu/business/mcfs/our-research/all-projects/climate-change/decarbonisation-credibility-benchmarking-framework"]," took a closer look at 16 of Australia’s largest ",["listed companies","https://www.asx.com.au/markets/trade-our-cash-market/directory"]," operating across the emissions-intensive metals, mining and energy sectors. This includes energy giants ",["BHP","https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/may/25/bhp-files-leak-mining-company-climate-action"]," and ",["Woodside","https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/25/woodside-scraps-emissions-clean-energy-targets-australia"],", both of which have recently made headlines for winding back their climate commitments."]},{"k":"p","s":["For each company, we reviewed publicly available information published between July 1 2024 and June 30 2025. Sources included annual reports, sustainability reports, climate reports, transition plans and sustainability data books."]},{"k":"p","s":["We assessed companies’ disclosures against a set of indicators to test the credibility of their net zero targets and performance metrics, such as reported greenhouse gas emissions. We also examined their implementation measures, including electrification and energy efficiency improvements, and the financial resources allocated to these measures."]},{"k":"p","s":["We focused on public information because it helps:"]},{"k":"li","s":["investors decide how to distribute their money"]},{"k":"li","s":["regulators evaluate how effective government policies are"]},{"k":"li","s":["community members hold companies to account for their climate action or lack thereof."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Global carbon emissions may have peaked in 2026 – but only time will tell","https://theconversation.com/global-carbon-emissions-may-have-peaked-in-2026-but-only-time-will-tell-296152"]]},{"k":"h","s":["The gap between ambition and action"]},{"k":"p","s":["There’s ",["evidence","https://ca1-nzt.edcdn.com/PDFs-and-Excels/Net_Zero_Stocktake_2026.pdf?v=1793874786"]," that many companies have kept their net zero targets in place despite political and economic challenges, such as the United States’ ",["second withdrawal","https://theconversation.com/trump-has-withdrawn-the-us-from-the-paris-agreement-heres-why-thats-not-such-a-bad-thing-248109"]," from the Paris Agreement and the ongoing ",["Middle East conflict","https://carnegieendowment.org/research/2026/09/iran-war-climate-environmental-human-security-fallout"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, our findings reveal a significant gap between companies’ reported net zero targets and the concrete actions they have publicly committed to take."]},{"k":"p","s":["All companies in our sample have set public net zero targets. Some have a ",["transition plan","https://climateworkscentre.org/resource/guide-to-credibility-for-corporate-climate-transition-plans/"]," – laying out the targets, actions and resources a company will use to reduce its emissions – and identify a broad set of measures to implement these targets."]},{"k":"p","s":["Each of the 16 companies cited ",["electrification","https://theconversation.com/the-world-needs-to-get-serious-about-electrification-heres-why-296062"]," and ",["fuel switching","https://partnersinprojectgreen.com/resources/mitigation-fuel-switching/"]," – replacing fossil fuel-based systems with renewables – as implementation measures. Improving energy efficiency was also common across 15 of the 16 companies studied. For example, ",["BlueScope Steel","https://www.bluescope.com/content/dam/bluescope/corporate/bluescope-com/sustainability/documents/fy2025/FY2025_BlueScope_Sustainability_Report.pdf"]," reported that upgrading industrial paint ovens at its Western Port facility in Victoria cut the company’s annual emissions by about 18,000 tonnes. All but two companies had ",["supply chain decarbonisation","https://netzerocompare.com/academy/a-comprehensive-guide-to-supply-chain-decarbonization"]," – the process of reducing or cutting carbon emissions produced at various stages of a supply chain – as a goal."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, many companies published limited quantitative data showing whether these measures would actually reduce their emissions. For example, Fortescue’s ",["2025 Climate Transition Plan","https://www.google.com/url?q=https://fy25ctp.fortescue.com/en&source=gmail&ust=1794542514470000&usg=AOvVaw3hXwlYI1dfrQvyW50suMDy"]," described efficiency initiatives without offering clear emissions reduction figures. What’s more, we found a major gap between companies’ stated decarbonisation commitments and the information they publicly disclosed about how they would pay for these efforts."]},{"k":"p","s":["Of the 16 companies studied, 11 claimed to have allocated funds for decarbonisation measures. However, only 7 companies disclosed how they calculated climate-related costs or considered them in their investment decisions. Rio Tinto, for instance, reports ",["it assessed","https://www.riotinto.com/en/invest/reports/annual-report"]," proposed investments against criteria including their potential to reduce emissions and financial costs. Just five of the 16 companies conducted post-investment reviews or audits."]},{"k":"p","s":["These discrepancies make it extremely difficult to know if company climate targets are contributing to corporate, national and global net zero goals."]},{"k":"p","s":["While all companies had room for improvement, some provided more detailed disclosures than others. Fortescue ",["forecast","https://content.fortescue.com/fortescue17114-fortescueeb60-productionbbdb-8be5/media/project/fortescueportal/shared/documents/publications/environment-publications/climate-transition-plan.pdf"]," spending US$700 million to US$900 million (A$1 billion to A$1.3 billion) on emissions reduction in 2025, but subsequently ",["reported","https://content.fortescue.com/fortescue17114-fortescueeb60-productionbbdb-8be5/media/project/fortescueportal/shared/documents/regulatory/asx-announcements/2935109-fy25-annual-report-and-appendix-4e.pdf"]," spending US$405 million (A$600 million). Disclosing both planned and actual expenditure offers insight into how companies are progressing, but doesn’t necessarily show whether their investments are enough to meet their climate targets."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["The world needs to get serious about electrification – here’s why","https://theconversation.com/the-world-needs-to-get-serious-about-electrification-heres-why-296062"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Disclosure is not enough"]},{"k":"p","s":["Australia’s new ",["mandatory climate disclosure","https://www.asic.gov.au/regulatory-resources/sustainability-reporting"]," system requires large Australian companies to provide climate-related financial information each year. They must submit this information alongside their annual reporting obligations, including greenhouse gas emissions and climate targets."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, disclosure alone will not give companies enough incentive to realise their net zero commitments."]},{"k":"p","s":["Governments must also introduce stronger policies that require companies to reduce emissions and invest in cleaner technologies. Australia’s ",["Safeguard Mechanism","https://lens.monash.edu/can-australias-safeguard-mechanism-deliver-the-emissions-cuts-it-promises/"],", the main federal tool for cutting emissions from big polluters, is one such example."]},{"k":"p","s":["Clearer international commitments can also help. Australia and other countries should support the development of a ",["global roadmap","https://www.carbonbrief.org/qa-what-is-in-the-global-roadmap-for-transitioning-away-from-fossil-fuels"]," for transitioning away from fossil fuels, proposed by Brazil at last year’s ",["COP30 summit","https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/nov/03/brazil-first-global-roadmap-phasing-out-fossil-fuels"],". This could provide greater certainty about the direction of the global transition and encourage companies to invest in greener technologies."]},{"k":"p","s":["Effective scrutiny by regulators, investors and the courts is also key to keeping companies accountable for their commitments."]},{"k":"p","s":["For too long, large companies have failed to make good on their climate commitments. More specific and robust reporting requirements will go some way to fixing this. And by scrutinising company claims, investors, researchers and the wider community can also help keep net zero within reach."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Extreme El Niños are coming. Reaching net zero sooner means facing fewer of them","https://theconversation.com/extreme-el-ninos-are-coming-reaching-net-zero-sooner-means-facing-fewer-of-them-292134"]]}],"chars":6365},"https://theconversation.com/grattan-on-friday-can-albanese-regain-political-altitude-for-labor-and-himself-294365":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"7eefccb2049af5869a7a1b420605c08290bd7336f57ac39660f905a9fc075a73","read":"https://theconversation.com/grattan-on-friday-can-albanese-regain-political-altitude-for-labor-and-himself-294365","bytes":179050,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Grattan on Friday: Can Albanese regain political altitude for Labor – and himself?","by":[{"n":"Michelle Grattan","r":"Professorial Fellow, University of Canberra"}],"pub":"2026-11-12T07:13:03Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["A government in trouble is like an aircraft in a dangerous plunge. It can be pulled out of the dive if its mechanical problems are fixable and the piloting sufficiently skilful. If those conditions are not met, however, the plane will crash land, with who knows what degree of damage."]},{"k":"p","s":["Anthony Albanese and his government have seriously lost altitude."]},{"k":"p","s":["We saw something similar before the 2025 election, and then the captain and crew didn’t just stabilise the plane – they flew it to an unexpected height. But every flight is a new journey."]},{"k":"p","s":["Albanese would use a different word picture. He recently told his worried caucus, “we’ll be kicking with the wind in the fourth quarter”."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s his old line and it proved true last time. But the wind direction in 2028 is unpredictable."]},{"k":"p","s":["What is clear is the shine has well and truly disappeared from Albanese’s leadership."]},{"k":"p","s":["Albanese was never a charismatic leader, neither a great orator nor an innovative policy thinker. He says people always underestimated him. Perhaps it was more a case of underestimating how far he could rise. He’s a superior tactician, honed in the fires of Labor’s left, with long experience in politics and in government. That gave him a competent skill set in his bid for the prime ministership. Fortuitous circumstances helped with the rest."]},{"k":"p","s":["In both 2022 and 2025 he benefitted less from having a tailwind than from his opponents facing strong headwinds. Voters wanted to dispatch Scott Morrison. Then they couldn’t stomach Peter Dutton."]},{"k":"p","s":["Albanese is in his present dire trouble because of multiple factors, some outside his control, others his own fault."]},{"k":"p","s":["Voters’ black mood reflects in large part the serious financial straits many families are in with the cost-of-living pressures and the real wages slump. Annual real wages are not forecast to begin growing again until towards the end of 2027."]},{"k":"p","s":["Albanese said in March 2025, “Australians have gone through a difficult time over the last five years. […] What we’ve done, as a fact is to introduce cost-of-living relief […] We are turning the corner. Australians now are getting real wage increases five quarters in a row. Interest rates have begun to fall. Inflation has declined to the lower half of the Reserve Bank band.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Voters see that narrative was quite wrong. They can’t, either, feel much effect from the cost-of-living relief. They’re unimpressed by declarations that the government feels their pain. Now they want to see what plan the government has to get the economy, and their personal financial lives, into a better place. Unfortunately that’s easier said than done."]},{"k":"p","s":["Albanese has played into people’s perception that the word of politicians can’t be trusted. His now notorious fall off a stage was nothing in itself, but his disputing that he did fall turned it into a damaging symbol. His poor judgement and stubbornness in dealing with the stage incident manifested again in his handling of the aftermath from the Bushie podcast in which he unthinkingly insulted the Japanese PM (although the initial judgement lapse was in agreeing to the podcast in the first place)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Albanese last term got away with breaking his promise not to change the stage three tax cuts. The reworking could be justified in the name of equity, and the breach was a one-off."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the May budget’s spectacular broken promises, on negative gearing and capital gains tax, crossed a tipping point. It now looked like a pattern. Albanese had been so emphatic during the campaign when questioned about these taxes. His rationalisation, “we have changed our position”, came across as frustratingly slick and unconvincing, indeed insulting, as if it had all been a clever con."]},{"k":"p","s":["The trust problem was worsened by the budget’s messy landing, necessitating concessions. The pluses and minuses of the shock to the housing sector are being hotly debated, with the longer term implications unclear."]},{"k":"p","s":["The post budget battle has been against a background of continuing high inflation culminating in five interest rate rises this year and increasing pressure on the government over its spending. Labor rejects claims of fiscal profligacy, but acknowledges they must be addressed in the December’s half-yearly budget update, and into 2027."]},{"k":"p","s":["Not always but typically, voters go through a cycle in their attitude to leaders. Initial positivity fades, replaced by boredom or negativity. Albanese was seen as a safe pair of hands, a benign well-intentioned leader, at a personal level always going on about his rugby league team and his fluffy white dog Toto. But now even many staunch Labor people are “over” him."]},{"k":"p","s":["He has never excelled at communication. Testing times accentuate his rambling at news conferences, his failure to directly answer difficult questions, a tendency to impatience. In opposition he preached the need for accountability and openness. This week one of his former press secretaries who has returned to journalism called him out for making announcements at news conferences before the reporters are given the relevant material that would allow them to ask informed questions. Control and secrecy are marks of this government."]},{"k":"p","s":["Those on the left complained in Albanese’s first term that he should be more of a “Labor reformer”. The strength of these calls (plus the size of the 2025 win) may have been important in leading him to go the whole hog and embrace the controversial tax agenda for the May budget."]},{"k":"p","s":["After a term and a half, the Hawke government had laid down some markers for its legacy, with a start on serious economic reform. In a similar timeframe, the Howard government was embarking on its sweeping tax shakeup."]},{"k":"p","s":["Where is Albanese’s legacy up to?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The first term was supposed to deliver the Voice as an enduring achievement. That failed, proving divisive and its defeat resulting in the government stepping back and leaving a void in indigenous policy."]},{"k":"p","s":["The 2026 budget was designed to build a legacy, in its significant realignment of taxation, away from benefitting investors and their assets and towards helping workers; a shift from older people to the younger generations. But it turned into an exploding cigar."]},{"k":"p","s":["Albanese is still to set up a credible legacy. Time is running out because, assuming he does win the 2028 election, he’d be expected to depart during the following term. In the meantime he has to find ways for that plane to steady and regain some altitude."]}],"chars":6361},"https://theconversation.com/david-ebys-early-election-call-backfires-badly-putting-conservatives-in-power-in-b-c-294928":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"06926b7e8b27780b0610026939b03d02d44472943619dd8cd90c806f1922c841","read":"https://theconversation.com/david-ebys-early-election-call-backfires-badly-putting-conservatives-in-power-in-b-c-294928","bytes":185570,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"David Eby’s early election call backfires badly, putting Conservatives in power in B.C.","by":[{"n":"Stewart Prest","r":"Lecturer, Political Science, University of British Columbia"}],"pub":"2026-10-25T13:57:31Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Conservative Lorne Doerkson, ",["a man who hadn’t even campaigned to be leader of his own party","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/british-columbia/lorne-doerkson-next-premier-5-reasons-9.7395150"],", will be British Columbia’s next premier after his party ",["won an election","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/british-columbia/livestory/bc-provincial-election-results-live-updates-2026-9.7389208"]," that didn’t need to be held against an opponent who largely defeated himself."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even in a province long accustomed to ",["unprecedented developments in its politics","https://doi.org/10.3138/chr.104.1.rev01"],", this was a remarkable turn of events. Just two years since B.C.’s last provincial election, in the middle of the province’s regularly scheduled municipal election campaign, Eby sent B.C. voters back to the polls early."]},{"k":"p","s":["Throughout the election, ",["Eby struggled to justify the call","https://www.richmond-news.com/economy-law-politics/rob-shaw-eby-cant-conjure-a-convincing-reason-to-call-snap-election-12812543"],". The initial explanation, offered at the start of the campaign, centred on the need for the province to draw a line in the sand against United States President Donald Trump."]},{"k":"p","s":["Later, during the leaders’ debate, Eby tried a new line."]},{"k":"p","s":["He focused instead on the ",["thinness of his one-seat majority","https://www.facebook.com/dave.eby/videos/a-one-seat-majority-meant-every-single-vote-could-bring-down-the-government-my-c/1422653296715906/"]," — which was nonetheless still a majority — and the challenges that came with its management amid MLA sickness and the untimely passing of long-time NDP MLA ",["Joan Philip","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/british-columbia/joan-phillip-dies-9.7325163"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Affordability, healthcare were top concerns"]},{"k":"p","s":["Neither of these justifications made much sense, however. There was nothing new in late September 2026 on the Trump front that required a provincial reset. And as much as ",["British Columbians agree that Trump is a problem","https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-10-23/british-columbia-s-eby-falls-behind-conservatives-as-anti-trump-strategy-falters"],", they evidently are looking to the federal government, rather than the provincial, to lead the country’s response."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Polls consistently showed provincial concerns were closer to home","https://angusreid.org/bc-election-polling-2026/"],", related to affordability and access to core government services, ",["particularly healthcare","https://www.doctorsofbc.ca/advocacy/2026/health-care-ranked-top-priority-british-columbians-ahead-provincial-election"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["As for the unmanageability of the legislature, a thin majority is still a majority. This explanation therefore seemed opportunistic given that other governments, including previous iterations of the NDP, have done much with less."]},{"k":"p","s":["These explanations rang all the more hollow given the obvious political motives behind the election call. The NDP had climbed back to a small lead in polls over the summer, and was facing a B.C. Conservative opposition in disarray."]},{"k":"p","s":["The new Conservative party leader at the time, ",["Kerry-Lynne Findlay, had made a number of controversial organizational moves, alienating much of her own party in the process","https://www.biv.com/news/commentary/rob-shaw-findlays-brief-reign-a-masterclass-in-political-self-destruction-12802331"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["By the weekend before the Sept. 22 election call, more than a dozen MLAs had either left or been expelled from the Conservative Party. Eight former Conservatives joined the nascent CentreBC party to create an alternative right-of-centre political vehicle."]},{"k":"p","s":["Simply put, the simplest explanation seemed to be that Eby saw his chance to carve out a larger majority against a weakened opposition, and took it — consequences be damned. It was in fact a transparently obvious and particularly brazen bit of political opportunism, and voters saw it as such."]},{"k":"h","s":["Hoisted on his own election"]},{"k":"p","s":["Once underway, the campaign proved demoralizing for voters and participants alike. The NDP’s initial script for the campaign focused not just on the need to stand up to Trump, but also on the elements of conservativism in the province that bore hallmarks of MAGA politics. Eby called out what he described as ",["Conservative parties cozying up to Trump.","https://www.bcndp.ca/action-for-you"]]},{"k":"p","s":["These tactics might have worked when Findlay was still the Conservative leader. Hers was a particularly chaotic brand of populist politics; she had even ",["hired political staff with ties to the Alberta separatist movement.","https://globalnews.ca/news/12045195/conservative-mla-wilson-quits-bc-caucus/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Unfortunately for Eby, the threat of an imminent election accomplished what nothing else seemingly could — a reconciliation among Conservatives. Amid steadily increasing internal pressure, Findlay stepped down the Sunday before the election call. Following the ",["hasty selection of Doerkson as interim leader","https://langleyadvancetimes.com/2026/09/21/b-c-conservatives-appoint-lorne-doerkson-interim-leader/"],", most Conservatives in exile returned to the party."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["David Eby’s big gamble: Why calling an early B.C. election could backfire","https://theconversation.com/david-ebys-big-gamble-why-calling-an-early-b-c-election-could-backfire-293528"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Doerkson was also nearly a perfect foil for not only Eby but his Conservative predecessor, Findlay. A member of the more moderate wing of conservativism in the province, ",["Doerkson was as comfortable as Eby talking about his dislike of Trump and his politics","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/british-columbia/lorne-doerkson-leader-bc-conservatives-election-season-9.7357295"],". He proved a folksy, relatable politician as well, someone who exuded openness."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contrary to Eby’s claims, he seemed ",["an unlikely Trojan horse for radical populist conservatism","https://www.ctvnews.ca/vancouver/article/eby-says-doerkson-a-trojan-horse-for-conservative-extremists-as-bc-campaign-wraps/"],". The NDP’s script was no longer working. The situation had changed and Eby had failed to adapt accordingly, ultimately handing the Conservatives a historic majority."]},{"k":"h","s":["Low voter turnout"]},{"k":"p","s":["Rather than dent Conservative support, the biggest effect of the NDP’s negative campaigning proved to be to depress turnout for the party."]},{"k":"p","s":["While a few ballots remain to be counted, ",["turnout in the election is unlikely to cross the 50 per cent threshold","https://dailyhive.com/vancouver/bc-provincial-election-advance-turnout-october-2026-statistics"],", which would represent one of the lowest turnouts in recorded B.C. election history."]},{"k":"p","s":["The NDP is on track to receive 250,000 fewer votes than in 2024, even as the Conservative vote total also declined slightly. In short, it seems more than a quarter of NDP voters simply stayed home this time around, unwilling to validate Eby’s unnecessary and polarizing election."]},{"k":"p","s":["Back in 2017, when he was the province’s attorney general, Eby was ",["tasked with cleaning up the province’s gambling industry","https://vancouversun.com/opinion/columnists/vaughn-palmer-eby-set-to-play-governments-cards-on-casino-crackdown"],". In 2026, as premier, Eby was the gambler. He bet the house on an unnecessary early election and he lost it all."]}],"chars":5274},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/guyana":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"22ed107ca32d0cff794b485f79f63ec1859fed153c6eca580f0e2d89fc36e6f3","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/guyana","bytes":49126,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Guyana travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-01-07T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2025-12-30T14:37:59+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/guyana/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Guyana’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Guyana set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the Guyana High Commission in the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Guyana, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will not be able to enter Guyana if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You do not need a visa to visit Guyana. Visitors can normally stay for 30 days, but you can apply for one-month extensions from Guyana’s ",["immigration and support services","https://eservices.iss.gov.gy/visitor-visa?new=1"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Guyanese authorities can arrest visitors who overstay or abuse the conditions of their stay. You could get a one-year prison sentence, a fine of up to 50,000 Guyana dollars (about 250 US dollars) and deportation – at your own expense – upon your release."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check the requirements for work or student visas with the Guyana High Commission in the UK well before you travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, including yellow fever, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Guyana guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/99/guyana#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Guyana. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Guyana"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Guyana, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are occasional protests and political demonstrations throughout Guyana. Stay away from demonstrations as unrest can occur without notice."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Border areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Venezuela disputes the legitimacy of its border with Guyana. Political tensions remain and the security situation along the border remains tense. There has also been an increase in organised criminality in these border areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["There continues to be a dispute between Suriname and Guyana over the land in the New River Triangle area in the south-east of Guyana."]},{"k":"p","s":["Organised crime in these border areas is common and increasing."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with local authorities if travelling near the border areas, both of which are in remote areas."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime levels are significant, and police capacity is low. Petty crime, including pickpocketing and bag snatching, is common, and violent crime continues to be a risk."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Violent attacks and personal safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks and muggings have occurred in broad daylight but are more common at night, and have included the use of knives or firearms. They may target tourists, particularly those that show obvious signs of wealth."]},{"k":"p","s":["Foreign and Guyanese nationals have reportedly been targeted in:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Stabroek Market in Georgetown"]},{"k":"li","s":["Tiger Bay and Albouystown in Georgetown"]},{"k":"li","s":["Sophia, south Georgetown"]},{"k":"li","s":["Buxton"]},{"k":"li","s":["Agricola"]},{"k":"p","s":["Foreign visitors have been assaulted in Georgetown’s Botanical Gardens. If possible, visit with an organised group and avoid taking valuables."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been incidents of gangs following cars from Cheddi Jagan International Airport and then attacking their victims when they reach their destination. Always drive with windows closed and doors locked."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care when exchanging money or buying goods on the street. Go inside the money exchange or shop, or use ATMs inside banks or shopping centres. Consider arranging to be collected by a car or taxi booked by your hotel or with a licensed operator."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Thieves will take items from hotel rooms, parked vehicles or luggage if it is unattended. Keep your passports, money, tickets, mobile phones and other valuables as secure as you can, and use hotel safes or safe deposit boxes if possible."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scams"]},{"k":"p","s":["Scammers often offer travellers in South America free air tickets to Guyana. On arrival their ‘sponsors’ will only allow them to leave Guyana if they carry a ‘package’ (usually cocaine). The authorities at the airport will stop and search foreigners that fit this known profile."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can get lengthy prison sentences and heavy fines for possession or the trafficking of drugs. The minimum jail sentence for drug offences is 3 years, and prison conditions in Guyana are tough. Pack all luggage yourself and do not carry any items that do not belong to you."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is illegal. In practice, these laws are rarely enforced, and there is growing local support for LGBT+ rights. You could receive negative attention for showing affection in public."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hotel safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fires have occurred in Guyanese hotels, and some hotels have poor fire safety procedures. Check evacuation procedures and exit routes when you arrive, and speak to hotel management if you have any concerns."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Guyana, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Guyana. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"],". After 60 days you’ll need to buy a ",["4-week foreign driving permit","https://www.gra.gov.gy/driving-with-a-foreign-licence/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re planning to hire a car, check with your car hire company for information on their requirements before you travel."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving standards and road conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving in Guyana can be dangerous because of reckless drivers, frequent hazards, poor street lighting, and poor road conditions. Drive with caution and take extreme care if you choose to drive at night. Keep a safe distance from minibuses – minibus drivers are responsible for many of the road accidents in Guyana."]},{"k":"p","s":["If possible, avoid travel to and from Cheddi Jagan International Airport late at night and before dawn. There have been fatal accidents caused by erratic driving."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis and minibuses"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although private taxis can be targeted by robbers, they are the safest way for visitors to get around Georgetown. Use taxis from reputable companies and book them in advance or from official hotel taxi ranks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not hail taxis from the roadside, and avoid using “public” minibuses unless pre-booked from reputable sources."]},{"k":"hs","s":["River and sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been armed attacks against fishing boats in and around the waters of Guyana and Suriname, and those between Guyana and Venezuela. If you’re travelling by sea, ",["read about the regional risks at sea","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/sea-river-and-piracy-safety"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are travelling on Guyana’s rivers, use registered boat services equipped with life jackets. Do not travel by boat after dark."]},{"k":"p","s":["Only use scheduled ferry services when crossing the Corentyne River between Guyana and Suriname. Using water taxis (‘backtracking’) from Suriname to Guyana is illegal and can lead to arrest, imprisonment and then deportation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["Guyana is vulnerable to flooding. The main rainy seasons are generally May to June and December to January. The coast of Guyana is below sea level and protected by a sea defence and dam system. However, the anti-flooding infrastructure and drainage systems are poorly maintained"]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 913 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Guyana","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/99/guyana#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Go to TravelHealthPro to see ",["what health risks you’ll face in Guyana","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/99/guyana"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["yellow fever"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["zika virus"]},{"k":"li","s":["oropouche Virus"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria in the interior of the country"]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Guyana. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2024, UNAIDS estimated that around 11,000 people in Guyana were living with HIV. Take normal precautions to avoid exposure to HIV/AIDS."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Guyana"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical facilities are very limited, even in Georgetown. There are extremely limited health facilities in remote areas. Standards of medical practice are low and you should arrange an evacuation for any serious or invasive treatment if possible. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Guyana","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/guyana-list-of-list-of-medical-facilities-practioners/list-of-medical-facilities-in-guyana"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Guyana"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 913"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 912"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 911"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Guyana"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Guyana"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Guyana"]," in Guyana"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Guyana","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/when-someone-dies-in-guyana"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Guyana","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/guyana-prisoner-pack/prisoner-pack-guyana"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/guyana/british-high-commission-georgetown"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/guyana/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Guyana","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-guyana"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":12826,"change":"Updated information on health risks and healthcare in Guyana (‘Health’ page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/malta":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"d39733d04981472d267c52d7bafabd65b1d60a04997f6d278b3679e8f9982297","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/malta","bytes":66325,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Malta travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-20T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-08-11T10:20:07+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/malta/email-signup"]," when this advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/travelaware/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Malta set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Maltese High Commission in the UK","https://foreigncms.gov.mt/en/Embassies/Hc_London/Pages/The-High-Commission.aspx"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Malta follows ",["Schengen area rules","https://europa.eu/youreurope/citizens/travel/entry-exit/non-eu-nationals/index_en.htm"],". Your passport must:"]},{"k":"li","s":["have a ‘date of issue’ less than 10 years before the date you arrive – if you renewed your passport before 1 October 2018, it might have a date of issue that is more than 10 years ago, making it invalid for entry to the Schengen area"]},{"k":"li","s":["have an ‘expiry date’ at least 3 months after the day you plan to leave the Schengen area (the expiry date does not need to be within 10 years of the date of issue)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can ",["travel without a visa to the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/travel-to-eu-schengen-area"],", which includes Malta, for up to 90 days in any 180-day period. This applies if you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["as a tourist"]},{"k":"li","s":["to visit family or friends"]},{"k":"li","s":["to attend business meetings, cultural or sports events"]},{"k":"li","s":["for short-term studies or training"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["requirements for working in Malta","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/travel-to-malta-for-work"]," are different."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are travelling to other Schengen countries as well, make sure your whole visit is within the 90-day limit. Visits to Schengen countries in the previous 180 days before you travel count towards your 90 days. If you overstay the 90-day visa-free limit, you may be banned from entering Schengen countries for up to 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["At Maltese border control, you may also need to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["show a return or onward ticket"]},{"k":"li","s":["prove that you have enough money for your stay"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Staying longer than 90 days in a 180-day period"]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer, you must meet the Maltese government’s entry requirements. Check which type of visa or permit you need with the ",["Maltese High Commission in the UK","https://foreigncms.gov.mt/en/Embassies/Hc_London/Pages/Visa-Advice-for-Foreign-Nationals.aspx"],". The ",["Maltese Central Visa Unit","https://identita.gov.mt/central-visa-unit-main-page/"]," also has information."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you stay in Malta with a residence permit or long-stay visa, this does not count towards your 90-day visa-free limit."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read about ",["entry processes if you live in Malta","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-malta#passports-and-travel"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["New Schengen entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["The European Union’s (EU) new Entry/Exit System (EES) is now being implemented across the Schengen area."]},{"k":"p","s":["This means that when you travel into the Schengen area for short stays, you may need to register your biometric details, such as fingerprints and a photo. There is no cost for EES registration."]},{"k":"p","s":["On your first visit into a Schengen country, you may be asked to register your details at a special booth before proceeding to the immigration desk. Follow directions from your travel operator or the staff at your port of entry. You may also need to provide either your fingerprint or photo when you leave the Schengen area. Children aged 11 or younger will not have their fingerprints scanned but can be required to have their photo taken."]},{"k":"p","s":["You do not need to take any action before you arrive at the border on entry to the Schengen area, but EES may take each passenger extra time to complete so be prepared to wait longer than usual at the border and to allow more time for immigration controls when you depart the Schengen area. If you are departing the Schengen area by plane, allow extra time to reach your departure gate as EES checks may take place before boarding."]},{"k":"p","s":["EES is replacing the previous system of manually stamping passports when visitors arrive in the Schengen area for short stays. You may be asked to input biometric details every time you enter or exit."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you enter the Schengen area through the Port of Dover, Eurotunnel at Folkestone or Eurostar at St Pancras International, any information will be taken at the border before you leave the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your digital EES record is valid for 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["information on the EU Entry/Exit System and to understand which countries are in the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/eu-entryexit-system"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are long-term resident in a Schengen country, you are exempt from EES in all Schengen countries. The full list of EES exemptions is on ",["the EU’s official Travel Europe website.","https://travel-europe.europa.eu/en/ees/to-whom-does-ees-not-apply"]]},{"k":"p","s":["If you believe you have been incorrectly entered into EES or your record of time spent in the Schengen area is incorrect, approach border officials when you next cross the Schengen border and request a correction. If you are exempt, carry documentation confirming your status. If you believe your time spent in the Schengen area has been recorded incorrectly, raise this with border officials and be prepared to provide supporting evidence if requested."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Malta, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Malta guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/141/malta#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods that can be brought into and taken out of Malta","https://customs.gov.mt/home"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking food into Malta"]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot take ",["meat, milk or products containing them into EU countries","https://ec.europa.eu/food/animals/animalproducts/personal_imports_en"],". There are some exceptions such as powdered baby milk, baby food and special foods or pet feed required for medical reasons."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Malta"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare cash or travellers cheques if the value is 10,000 euros or more. You will get a certified declaration to show you brought it in with you. If you do not, your money could be seized when you leave."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Malta"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Malta, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should be aware of the global risk of indiscriminate terrorist attacks, which could be in public places, including those visited by foreigners."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime against tourists is rare, but there have been incidents of:"]},{"k":"li","s":["robbery"]},{"k":"li","s":["handbag snatching"]},{"k":"li","s":["pickpocketing"]},{"k":"li","s":["theft from parked cars"]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce your risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["be cautious when exchanging money and using ATMs"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid carrying large amounts of cash if possible"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not keep all your valuables in one place"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep a copy of your passport somewhere safe"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pickpocketing has happened on bus routes between Valletta and St Julian’s. Thieves target crowded buses during the summer season. Always keep sight of valuables."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink and food spiking"]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminals have drugged people in some bars and gentlemen’s clubs in the Paceville district. They’ve forced them to spend large amounts of money or assaulted them. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["be careful who you buy drinks from"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep drinks in sight to make sure they are not spiked"]},{"k":"li","s":["check your bill to make sure you are not being overcharged"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been assaults, including rape and sexual assault. Avoid splitting up from your friends and do not go off with people you do not know. If you drink, take sensible precautions including buying your own drinks and always keeping sight of them."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scams"]},{"k":"p","s":["Scams targeting British nationals are increasing. These come in many forms (romance and friendship, business ventures, work and employment opportunities) and can pose financial risk to victims."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be cautious about any requests for money, a job offer, a business venture or a face-to-face meeting from someone you met over the internet."]},{"k":"p","s":["For more information, see guidance from ",["ActionFraud","https://www.actionfraud.police.uk/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Bird hunting seasons"]},{"k":"p","s":["Bird hunting takes place in the spring and autumn. The Maltese government decides the dates at the start of each season. See local print and online media for the dates and times when hunting is allowed."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hunting with firearms is common. It is normally allowed from 2 hours before sunrise until 2 hours after sunset. Hunting areas are rarely marked and can overlap with camping areas, country walkways and other public areas. Although not common, there have been incidents between members of the public and locals. Be aware of your surroundings when visiting rural areas and nature spots during the hunting seasons."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal drugs, including cannabis, carry severe penalties for tourists."]},{"k":"p","s":["Malta legalised the cultivation and personal use of cannabis at home in 2021, but smoking in public is illegal and attracts a fine. Possession of up to 7g of cannabis in public for personal use at home is legal for Maltese residents only."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for possessing, using or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through the airport. Schengen bans (of up to 5 years) may also be issued alongside fines or after release from detention."]},{"k":"p","s":["The airport in Malta has excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming and beaches"]},{"k":"p","s":["Every year, people drown in the sea and in swimming pools in Malta."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming pools"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always supervise children. Keep small children within arms-reach in and around swimming pools, even if they can swim or there is a lifeguard present."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Beaches"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care when swimming in the sea. Always supervise children and keep small children within arms-reach. Some beaches may have strong undercurrents."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hidden rocks or shallow depths can cause serious injury or death. Do not dive into unknown water and do not swim at beaches where a river runs into the sea."]},{"k":"p","s":["During the summer, lifeguards patrol most beaches and use a flag safety system. Make sure you understand the system and follow any warnings. Red flags indicate dangerous or hazardous conditions. Swim within designated zones and take extra care if there are no lifeguards, flags or signs. If you are walking along unmonitored beaches, be aware that waves can come in further than expected and have strong undertows."]},{"k":"p","s":["See further tips on ",["ABTA’s swim safe pages","https://www.abta.com/tips-and-advice/staying-safe-on-holiday/swim-safe"]," and ",["Water Safety on Holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow local advice if jellyfish are present."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Malta, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and check the ",["rules of the road in the RAC’s Malta guide","https://www.rac.co.uk/drive/travel/country/malta"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other legal requirements you need to be aware of."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Malta. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on driving if you’re living in Malta","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-malta#driving-in-malta"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check if you need a ",["UK sticker to drive your car outside the UK","https://www.gov.uk/displaying-number-plates/flags-identifiers-and-stickers"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use your ",["Blue Badge in Malta","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/blue-badge-using-it-in-the-eu/using-a-blue-badge-in-the-european-union"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care while driving as some roads are in poor condition. Keep to the speed limit. Local standards of driving are poor."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 112 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the ",["latest vaccine recommendations for Malta","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/141/malta#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Malta","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/141/malta"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK prescriptions are not recognised in Malta. If you need medication while travelling, speak to a Maltese medical practitioner. A Maltese pharmacist can issue prescriptions from EU member states if they can confirm the prescriber is licensed."]},{"k":"p","s":["Medication in Malta might not match UK or EU makes and brands. Check your prescription has a suitable local equivalent with a pharmacist or doctor. A Maltese medical practitioner may need to assess you and issue a local prescription."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Malta"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Malta","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/malta-list-of-medical-facilitiespractitioners/list-of-medical-facilities-in-malta"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can request to see a private GP at most pharmacies."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Health insurance cards"]},{"k":"p","s":["To get medically necessary state healthcare in Malta, you need a Global Health Insurance Card (GHIC) or a European Health Insurance Card (EHIC)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The NHS’s ",["getting healthcare abroad webpage","https://www.nhs.uk/using-the-nhs/healthcare-abroad/apply-for-a-free-uk-global-health-insurance-card-ghic/"]," has details about:"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to apply for a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to get temporary cover if you lose your card or it does not arrive in time"]},{"k":"li","s":["who qualifies for a new EHIC instead of a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["what treatment counts as medically necessary"]},{"k":"p","s":["A GHIC or EHIC is not an alternative to travel insurance. You may have costs your GHIC or EHIC does not cover, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["changes to travel and accommodation bookings"]},{"k":"li","s":["additional standard costs for treatment"]},{"k":"li","s":["medical repatriation to the UK"]},{"k":"li","s":["treatment that is ruled non-urgent"]},{"k":"li","s":["private healthcare"]},{"k":"li","s":["private clinics"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Malta","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/healthcare-in-malta"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Malta"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 112 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Malta"]," and ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Malta"]," in Malta"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Malta","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/malta-bereavement-guide/malta-bereavement-information"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Malta","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/malta-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/malta/british-high-commission-malta"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/malta/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":16284,"change":"Updated information on European Entry-Exit System (EES) (‘Entry requirements’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/time-is-running-out-to-protect-franz-josef-from-its-rising-river-stopbanks-wont-work-forever-295959":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"15129b934c7b87a0c4080acff73d1a98e8bf55ffc78f72916fa230459306affd","read":"https://theconversation.com/time-is-running-out-to-protect-franz-josef-from-its-rising-river-stopbanks-wont-work-forever-295959","bytes":187333,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Time is running out to protect Franz Josef from its rising river. Stopbanks won’t work forever","by":[{"n":"Ian Christopher Fuller","r":"Professor in Physical Geography, Te Kunenga ki Pūrehuroa – Massey University"},{"n":"Tim Davies","r":"Adjunct Professor of Disaster Risk and Resilience, University of Canterbury"}],"pub":"2026-11-10T23:14:03Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Each year, more than a ",["million visitors pass through","https://www.westlanddc.govt.nz/recreation/places-to-visit/franz-josef-glacier/"]," the small South Island township of Franz Josef/Waiau on their way to see the West Coast’s glaciers and world heritage sites."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the town faces a rising flood risk because it sits beside one of the country’s most dynamic rivers."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Waiho River carries enormous quantities of gravel from the Southern Alps. As it leaves the mountains, it would naturally deposit gravel across a wide area, changing course over time."]},{"k":"p","s":["But since the 1980s, stopbanks (artificial levees) have confined the river to about a third of its natural bed, causing gravel to build up instead of spreading. As a result, the riverbed is rising by about 20 centimetres a year, three times faster than it would naturally."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2023, as members of the independent Waiho Technical Advisory Group, we warned that the rapidly rising riverbed posed an increasing threat to the town."]},{"k":"p","s":["We recommended a ",["ten-year plan","https://www.wcrc.govt.nz/repository/libraries/id:2459ikxj617q9ser65rr/hierarchy/Documents/Community/Consultation/Waiho%20River%20%E2%80%93%20Future%20Management%20Strategy/2023_Waiho%20TAG_Future%20Management%20of%20the%20Waiho%20River_Report.pdf"]," centred on giving the river more room to move and deposit its gravel, rather than relying on ever-higher stopbanks."]},{"k":"p","s":["The physics is simple: feeding the same amount of gravel into a smaller area makes the riverbed rise faster. As the riverbed rises, the safety margin provided by the stopbanks shrinks."]},{"k":"p","s":["When the group ",["reconvened","https://www.wcrc.govt.nz/repository/libraries/id:2459ikxj617q9ser65rr/hierarchy/Documents/Community/Consultation/Waiho%20River%20%E2%80%93%20Future%20Management%20Strategy/Waiho%20TAG%20Addendum%20report%202026%20FINAL.pdf"]," in August this year to review progress, we found the river was changing faster than the plan was being implemented."]},{"k":"p","s":["Time is running out fast. Keeping the town safe will require an approach to river management that offers lessons for other communities in New Zealand and around the world facing similar challenges."]},{"k":"h","s":["A river finding a new path"]},{"k":"p","s":["Since 2010, the Waiho has increasingly spilled north into the neighbouring Tatare Stream, which is about ten metres lower. From January 2023, this spill has carved out a new channel capturing ever more of the Waiho flow."]},{"k":"p","s":["Between March 2025 and March 2026, the spillover point moved a kilometre upstream and the new channel cut down by two metres, exceeding modelled predictions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Erosion along the new channel has already undermined the base of Havill’s Wall, which protects the town’s wastewater treatment ponds. But the Tatare channel is also filling with sediment. Once it is full, possibly within a decade, the Waiho is expected to reoccupy its southern bed."]},{"k":"p","s":["Large quantities of gravel also remain upstream, ready to move during future storms."]},{"k":"p","s":["An earthquake along the Alpine fault will compound the problem, damaging stopbanks and triggering landslides that deliver additional gravel into the river, accelerating the riverbed rise."]},{"k":"h","s":["The uncomfortable solution"]},{"k":"p","s":["The obvious response to a rising riverbed has been to build higher stopbanks. But that treats the symptom, not the cause. While the river remains confined, its bed will continue to rise rapidly and the banks will need to keep pace."]},{"k":"p","s":["Recent stopbank raising has temporarily reduced the likelihood of flooding, but not its potential consequences. With the river sitting higher above surrounding land, any breach will release floodwater with ",["catastrophic results","https://www.rnz.co.nz/national/programmes/afternoons/audio/2019058419/how-worried-should-we-be-about-franz-josef"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our central conclusion in 2023 was counterintuitive but logical: protecting Franz Josef/Waiau requires giving the Waiho more room."]},{"k":"p","s":["Releasing the river across its western floodplain would allow gravel to spread over a much larger area, slowing the rate of increase of pressure on the stopbanks protecting Franz Josef/Waiau."]},{"k":"h","s":["Nobody owns the problem"]},{"k":"p","s":["Making room for the Waiho will not be simple."]},{"k":"p","s":["It would mean relocating part of State Highway 6, the critical lifeline and main tourist road connecting communities along the West Coast, and removing landfills, farms and other infrastructure on the western flats."]},{"k":"p","s":["These actions formed part of the ten-year programme we recommended in 2023. Three years on, land purchases and relocation have not started, while highway planning remains at an early stage."]},{"k":"p","s":["Continuing delays mean stopbanks have to be raised further, with associated costs and increased risks, while the consequences of stopbank failure worsen incrementally."]},{"k":"p","s":["Part of the issue is governance. Flood protection, land-use planning, managed retreat, emergency management and local infrastructure all sit with different organisations. No single body is responsible for delivering the whole plan."]},{"k":"p","s":["We propose a new group led by Westland District Council and including the West Coast Regional Council and central government agencies, with a mandate to accelerate the work and pursue government funding."]},{"k":"p","s":["Franz Josef/Waiau is an early test of a question communities in New Zealand and elsewhere already face, and will face repeatedly in the future. Who leads, and who pays, when relocating property and infrastructure is the safest response to a growing natural hazard risk?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Independent experts have warned since 2002 that the traditional approach of raising stopbanks cannot continue. What is missing is not more information, but ownership and funding. Without both, the river will make the decision for us."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authors acknowledge the contribution by Matthew Gardner, Director at Land River Sea Consulting and Mark Healey, principal engineer (rivers) at WSP."]}],"chars":5046},"https://theconversation.com/poutine-menace-washington-inquiete-qui-protegera-leurope-295684":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-18T17:08Z","sha":"70cf1bc1f21ced9dbfa9b265a583df93d0651d77d4b114ebd7c89b26cec3ef0d","read":"https://theconversation.com/poutine-menace-washington-inquiete-qui-protegera-leurope-295684","bytes":185728,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Poutine menace, Washington inquiète : qui protégera l’Europe ?","by":[{"n":"Laurent Vilaine","r":"Docteur en sciences de gestion, ancien officier, enseignant en géopolitique à ESDES Business School, ESDES - UCLy (Lyon Catholic University)"}],"pub":"2026-11-18T15:38:36Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["L’ESSENTIEL"]},{"k":"li","s":["La France et le Royaume-Uni renforcent leur coopération nucléaire face à la menace russe et aux incertitudes sur l’engagement américain."]},{"k":"li","s":["L’exercice Rummy, en octobre 2026, a marqué une première avec la participation de chasseurs britanniques à un entraînement nucléaire aérien français."]},{"k":"li","s":["Cette coopération donne corps à l’idée d’une défense nucléaire européenne élargie, mais la crédibilité de cette solidarité reste à construire."]},{"k":"p","s":["Le 2 mars 2026, dans son fameux ",["discours de l’île Longue","https://www.elysee.fr/emmanuel-macron/2026/03/02/deplacement-sur-la-base-operationnelle-de-lile-longue"],", Emmanuel Macron a proposé d’étendre la profondeur stratégique de la dissuasion française au continent européen – ce qu’il a appelé une « dissuasion avancée » – et, notamment, d’associer des partenaires européens aux exercices nucléaires français."]},{"k":"p","s":["En outre, le chef de l’État a évoqué la possibilité de déployer ponctuellement des éléments des forces stratégiques françaises chez des alliés européens, ainsi que celle d’associer des forces conventionnelles alliées aux activités nucléaires françaises. Le président est cependant resté fidèle à l’orthodoxie nucléaire française dans la mesure où la décision d’emploi demeurera l’apanage de Paris. La proposition française, à ce jour, intéresse dix pays européens. Désormais, au-delà des discours, l’ouverture européenne de la France doit progresser par des coopérations opérationnelles."]},{"k":"p","s":[["L’exercice Rummy","https://www.gov.uk/government/news/uk-france-deepen-nuclear-defence-ties-in-first-joint-exercise"],", conduit les 20 et 21 octobre 2026, est une bonne illustration de ce rapprochement opérationnel. Pour la première fois, des Typhoon de la Royal Air Force ont participé à un exercice nucléaire aérien français. Les aéronefs britanniques escortaient des Rafale, ne portant pas d’armes nucléaires, simulant une mission de frappe nucléaire au-dessus de la Méditerranée. La mission à proprement parler nucléaire relevait de la composante aéroportée française, les appareils britanniques apportant un soutien conventionnel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Cet entraînement entre les deux puissances nucléaires du continent invite à s’interroger sur leur contribution à la sécurité des autres pays européens. En s’entraînant conjointement dans le cadre d’exercices opérationnels concrets, les armées britannique et française donnent une traduction tangible à leur solidarité stratégique, ce dont l’ensemble du continent peut bénéficier."]},{"k":"h","s":["Une coopération pensée à l’échelle européenne"]},{"k":"p","s":["Le 10 juillet 2025, Paris et Londres ont signé la ",["déclaration de Northwood","https://www.elysee.fr/emmanuel-macron/2025/07/10/declaration-de-la-republique-francaise-et-du-royaume-uni-de-grande-bretagne-et-dirlande-du-nord-sur-la-politique-et-la-cooperation-nucleaire"],". Les deux capitales y reconnaissent que, si leurs forces nucléaires sont indépendantes, elles peuvent néanmoins être coordonnées. Elles affirment surtout une grande solidarité dans la mesure où le texte précise qu’« il n’existe pas de menace extrême contre l’Europe qui ne susciterait pas de réponse de nos deux nations »."]},{"k":"p","s":["Le périmètre politique revendiqué ne s’arrête donc pas aux deux pays, mais comprend la sécurité du continent. La formulation laisse néanmoins ouverte la nature de la réponse, qui n’est pas nécessairement nucléaire, conformément au flou qui sied à toute posture défensive. La déclaration de Northwood et le discours de l’île Longue relèvent ainsi de démarches convergentes. La coordination franco-britannique est envisagée comme pouvant contribuer à un ensemble plus large de coopérations européennes, les engagements exacts restant toutefois à préciser."]},{"k":"p","s":["Cette contribution des deux pays à la défense collective n’a pas émergé ex nihilo. Elle possède déjà un fondement doctrinal. En effet, l’Otan (dont les deux pays comptent parmi les membres fondateurs en 1949) ",["reconnaît un rôle propre aux forces nucléaires françaises et britanniques","https://www.nato.int/en/what-we-do/deterrence-and-defence/natos-nuclear-deterrence-policy-and-forces"],", qui sont régulièrement citées comme participant à la sécurité globale de l’Alliance. Son importance réside dans le fait que l’existence de centres de décision distincts complique le calcul d’un adversaire. Dès lors, l’enjeu actuel est de donner davantage de contenu opérationnel à cette contribution, tout en préservant des autorités nationales capables de décider séparément."]},{"k":"h","s":["La menace russe et le coût du doute"]},{"k":"p","s":["La guerre déclenchée par la Russie contre l’Ukraine a replacé la coercition nucléaire au cœur des préoccupations européennes. Dès juin 2022, le ",["concept stratégique de l’Otan","https://www.nato.int/content/dam/nato/webready/documents/publications-and-reports/strategic-concepts/2022/290622-strategic-concept-fr.pdf"]," évoquait la menace russe en pointant la volonté de Moscou d’employer la force et d’envoyer des signaux nucléaires coercitifs. Un ",["autre document de l’Otan","https://www.etterretningen.no/2022/11/30/russias-nuclear-coercion-in-ukraine"],", publié en novembre 2022, explique que la rhétorique nucléaire russe cherche notamment à décourager une intervention de l’Alliance. Dans ce cadre, la difficulté pour les Européens est de faire face à ces intimidations et de préserver leur liberté d’action. La peur d’une escalade ne doit pas les diviser ou paralyser leur soutien à un partenaire."]},{"k":"p","s":["Paris et Londres inscrivent explicitement leur rapprochement dans ce contexte de réponse aux tentatives russes d’intimidation. Dans une ",["déclaration du 4 mars 2026","https://www.gov.uk/government/news/statement-by-the-united-kingdom-on-uk-france-nuclear-policy-and-cooperation"],", les gouvernements britannique et français affirment leur détermination à dissuader les menaces contre l’Europe et leur refus de se laisser influencer d’une quelconque manière par la rhétorique nucléaire russe. Le point important de cette annonce est la confirmation que la coopération franco-britannique ne vise pas seulement la protection des deux États, mais également celle de l’ensemble du continent."]},{"k":"p","s":["Rummy peut être interprété comme un signal de cette détermination de couverture continentale. Les deux États ont alors affiché leur coopération de manière très claire. Il ne s’agit plus d’intégrer cette volonté de coopération dans la doctrine, mais de la démontrer de manière opérationnelle, sur le terrain. Dès lors, les Russes sont contraints d’intégrer dans leurs calculs la possibilité d’une coordination franco-britannique en réaction à une agression venue de Moscou. Néanmoins, la prudence reste nécessaire. En effet, les informations publiques ne permettent pas de connaître l’appréciation russe de l’exercice et donc de mesurer son effet dissuasif."]},{"k":"p","s":["Au-delà, Rummy doit être replacé dans un ensemble plus large. Les Européens se réarment et soutiennent les Ukrainiens avec détermination. La montée des capacités conventionnelles européennes et l’intensification de la coopération nucléaire sur le continent obligent les Russes à en évaluer les conséquences sur leur posture et leurs éventuelles actions futures."]},{"k":"h","s":["Le changement américain accélère la posture européenne"]},{"k":"p","s":["La difficulté des Européens est qu’ils doivent réfléchir aux évolutions de leur posture de défense, non seulement en raison de l’agressivité russe, mais également d’un fait absolument nouveau : le manque de confiance qu’inspire l’administration états-unienne. En cas d’agression russe contre un pays de l’Otan, est-on vraiment sûr de la disponibilité de l’appui américain ? Des éléments de doctrine et les déclarations gouvernementales américaines produisent une ambiguïté forte. La ",["stratégie de défense américaine de 2026","https://media.defense.gov/2026/Jan/23/2003864773/-1/-1/0/2026-NATIONAL-DEFENSESTRATEGY.PDF"]," insiste sur le fait que les alliés européens doivent assumer la responsabilité principale de leur défense conventionnelle. Le soutien des États-Unis est certes réaffirmé, mais plus limité qu’auparavant en raison de la priorité donnée à la défense du territoire américain et à la Chine."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["La Stratégie de sécurité nationale des États-Unis : 2022 contre 2025, continuités et ruptures","https://theconversation.com/la-strategie-de-securite-nationale-des-etats-unis-2022-contre-2025-continuites-et-ruptures-276223"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Dans une ",["note d’octobre 2026","https://eprs.europarl.europa.eu/EPRS_BRI(2026)796986?locale=EN"],", le service de recherche du Parlement européen met en exergue les inquiétudes que suscitent les messages politiques divergents de l’administration américaine et l’imprévisibilité des engagements de Washington. Malgré les engagements formels ",["réitérés lors du sommet d’Ankara du 8 juillet 2026","https://www.nato.int/en/about-us/official-texts-and-resources/official-texts/2026/07/08/the-ankara-summit-declaration"]," et en dépit de ",["l’inflexion que pourrait susciter la victoire démocrate aux midterms du 3 novembre 2026","https://theconversation.com/ce-quun-congres-domine-par-les-democrates-changerait-pour-leurope-295713"],", il n’est pas exagéré d’avancer que la confiance est rompue entre les Européens et les Américains."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lorsque la confiance s’effrite, un allié peut s’interroger sur les conditions de sa protection. Plus grave encore, un adversaire peut être tenté de tester la solidité de l’alliance. Dans ce cadre, les Européens n’ont d’autres choix que d’approfondir leur coopération et de réduire leur dépendance vis-à-vis d’un allié incertain."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ce qu’un exercice peut rendre plus crédible"]},{"k":"p","s":["Le soutien conventionnel à une mission nucléaire alliée n’est pas une invention de Rummy. L’Otan ",["prévoit déjà de telles contributions","https://www.nato.int/en/what-we-do/deterrence-and-defence/natos-nuclear-deterrence-policy-and-forces"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["En revanche, la principale nouveauté de l’exercice d’octobre réside dans la participation de chasseurs britanniques à un exercice nucléaire aérien français. La composante aérienne se prête particulièrement bien à ce type de démonstration de force, qui permet de rendre visible la coopération stratégique entre les deux pays."]},{"k":"p","s":["En septembre 2026, un ",["rapport du Sénat sur la dissuasion avancée","https://www.senat.fr/rap/r25-950/r25-950_mono.html"]," rappelle l’avantage de la composante nucléaire aérienne : sa visibilité et sa réversibilité, c’est-à-dire la capacité de rappeler un raid avant le lancement des armes. Outre ces caractéristiques classiques, il est également souligné que cette composante est particulièrement adaptée pour associer aux exercices des partenaires non dotés, ce qui rend la solidarité perceptible."]},{"k":"h","s":["La place des partenaires européens"]},{"k":"p","s":["L’efficacité du rapprochement franco-britannique dépendra aussi de l’association des partenaires non nucléaires. ",["Le communiqué franco-allemand du 17 juillet 2026","https://www.elysee.fr/emmanuel-macron/2026/07/17/conclusions-du-conseil-franco-allemand-de-defense-et-de-securite-du-17-juillet-2026"]," est éclairant à cet égard dans la mesure où il prévoit un dialogue sur l’articulation entre forces conventionnelles, défense antimissile et dissuasion française. Il donne également une traduction concrète à la dissuasion avancée proposée par la France en mars 2026. En effet, le ",["déploiement d’un Rafale à Nörvenich, en Allemagne","https://www.bfmtv.com/economie/economie-social/union-europeenne/un-rafale-dans-une-escadre-allemande-en-route-vers-la-fusion-nucleaire-developper-une-ia-de-frontiere-ce-qu-il-faut-retenir-du-dernier-sommet-franco-allemand_AV-202607170529.html"],", apparaît comme une première étape opérationnelle et annonce une participation conventionnelle allemande à un exercice nucléaire français."]},{"k":"p","s":["Les partenaires de la France dans le cadre de la dissuasion avancée peuvent donc apporter des moyens utiles sans acquérir l’arme nucléaire. Certes, des questions demeurent : quelle place auront-ils dans la discussion des risques ? Participer à un entraînement, fournir un soutien conventionnel et accepter une mission en période de crise constituent des engagements différents. Néanmoins, si l’on compare la contribution européenne à la défense du continent à ce qu’elle était il y a cinq ans, on constate que des pas énormes ont été accomplis."]},{"k":"p","s":["Soulignons que, tant du côté français que du côté britannique, l’emploi de l’arme nucléaire reste une prérogative ",["strictement nationale","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/defence-nuclear-enterprise-2026-annual-update-to-parliament/defence-nuclear-enterprise-2026-annual-update-to-parliament"],". De plus, les Britanniques rappellent que les coopérations européennes en matière de nucléaire ne font pas disparaître la coopération avec les États-Unis."]},{"k":"p","s":["Un exercice comme Rummy, auquel il faut désormais ajouter le début de concrétisation de la dissuasion avancée proposée par les Français, a un énorme avantage : nous rentrons dans une période de démonstration opérationnelle au-delà des déclarations. La dimension européenne de la défense nucléaire du territoire devient plus tangible face à la coercition russe et à l’imprévisibilité américaine. Il convient néanmoins de rester prudent : le futur de la crédibilité de la posture européenne reposera sur la cohérence entre les capacités exercées et les responsabilités que les parties prenantes seront prêtes à assumer."]}],"chars":11062},"https://theconversation.com/its-time-for-scientists-to-boycott-the-climate-cops-and-the-ipcc-297279":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-23T21:40Z","sha":"0b39f1df00ada666daa366c316079e1a7b879555085658c4f1b4281a9b8d18da","read":"https://theconversation.com/its-time-for-scientists-to-boycott-the-climate-cops-and-the-ipcc-297279","bytes":179626,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"It’s time for scientists to boycott the climate COPs and the IPCC","by":[{"n":"Andrew Weaver","r":"Professor, School of Earth and Ocean Sciences, University of Victoria"}],"pub":"2026-11-23T20:59:37Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["On Nov. 22, the day after ",["COP31 climate talks collapsed in Antalya","https://theconversation.com/how-did-the-cop31-climate-agreement-fall-apart-and-what-happens-now-296994"],", Turkey, the global average temperature at noon UTC was estimated to be a record-setting ",["2.36 C above the pre-industrial average","https://www.celsius.earth/motion/ridgeline"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Climate change is driving up global temperatures. Yet governments could not even agree to name the fossil fuels driving it."]},{"k":"p","s":["I have been a climate scientist since the late 1980s and have followed every UN climate summit since the ",["1992 Earth Summit","https://www.un.org/en/conferences/environment/rio1992"]," in Rio de Janeiro. I cannot recall a more embarrassing failure than COP31."]},{"k":"p","s":["The first draft proposed at least US$120 billion by 2035 to help countries adapt to climate change. By Nov. 19, the figure was gone."]},{"k":"p","s":["Three years ago in Dubai, governments agreed to transition away from fossil fuels. The ",["Nov. 16 Antalya draft","https://unfccc.int/sites/default/files/resource/dt_cop31_cover_decision.pdf"]," said so plainly. Yet, the ",["final proposal at COP31","https://www.carbonbrief.org/cop31-key-outcomes-agreed-at-the-un-climate-talks-in-antalya"]," still omitted any mention of fossil fuels. The European Union and small island states were right to reject it."]},{"k":"p","s":["Given the recent failure, is it time for scientists and activists to boycott COP?"]},{"k":"h","s":["From early success to utter failure"]},{"k":"p","s":["While COP31 collapsed without an agreement, previous UN climate talks have had successes. In the 1997 Kyoto Protocol, industrialized countries agreed to reduce their collective emissions, averaged over 2008–12, to 5.2 per cent below 1990 levels. Emissions over the 2008-12 reporting period came in ",["9.9 per cent below 1990 levels","https://www.ourcommons.ca/documentviewer/en/44-1/RNNR/meeting-11/evidence#Int-11571582"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":[["In Paris in 2015","https://unfccc.int/files/home/application/pdf/decision1cp21.pdf"],", governments agreed to hold warming “well below 2 C above pre-industrial levels” while “pursuing efforts to limit the temperature increase to 1.5 C above pre-industrial levels.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet, in June 2026, a UN report found that the world is ",["set to exceed","https://theconversation.com/yes-passing-1-5-c-of-global-warming-is-cause-for-alarm-but-not-despair-291331"]," the 1.5 C global warming target outlined in Paris."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2015, governments invited the Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change (IPCC) to report back in 2018 on the impacts of 1.5 C of warming and the emissions pathways that could get us there. ",["In future emissions pathways","https://www.ipcc.ch/sr15/chapter/spm/"]," leading to little or no overshoot of the 1.5 C target, global net carbon dioxide emissions were required to fall roughly 45 per cent from 2010 levels by 2030 and reach net zero around 2050."]},{"k":"p","s":["Those pathways also required removing 100 to 1,000 billion tonnes of carbon dioxide from the atmosphere over the century (so-called negative emissions) using technology that had yet to be developed. The authors spelled out the difficulties. The key government takeaway was that meeting the 1.5 C target could still be achieved."]},{"k":"p","s":["What struck me was how little those models resembled the world in which people make decisions. You can write carbon removal into a model. Somebody still has to find the land, build the equipment and pay to operate it. You don’t build a coal plant today to tear it down tomorrow. The utility has debt to repay and communities need power."]},{"k":"h","s":["What if we stayed home?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Scientists, environmentalists and youth groups should boycott the next COP. I further think scientists should also consider walking away from the Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change assessments."]},{"k":"p","s":["I was a ",["lead author on four of them","https://www.andrewjweaver.ca/biography/"],". I know what that invitation means to a young scientist, yet at some point, the scientific community needs to speak out as a collective. And those of us who have already had the privilege of working on IPCC assessments ought to speak first — and loudest."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Paris Agreement showed how readily governments can use our willingness to buy time. Ministers agreed on a temperature, asked us what it would mean if the world exceeded it, then continued exploiting fossil fuels regardless."]},{"k":"p","s":["Climate change has become a global tragedy of the commons."]},{"k":"p","s":["Fossil-fuel producers earn money ",["selling their products","https://theconversation.com/fossil-fuel-propaganda-is-stalling-climate-action-heres-what-we-can-do-about-it-272227"]," while sharing the climatic cost with everyone else. Countries and tech companies are incentivized to race ahead with artificial intelligence, ",["regardless of the environmental risks the rest of us inherit","https://theconversation.com/data-centres-may-consume-far-more-water-than-developers-suggest-296245"],". And in our politics, climate change has become subsumed into a culture war where politics rail against green policies regardless of the facts."]},{"k":"p","s":["While Canada’s delegates were in Antalya, Ottawa committed ",["$200 million","https://www.canada.ca/en/natural-resources-canada/news/2026/11/canada-invests-to-diversify-trade-create-jobs-and-lower-global-emissions-by-expanding-low-carbon-lng-exports.html"]," to expand planned production at Woodfibre LNG, a liquefied natural gas export terminal in British Columbia. With decisions like that, the world is on course to even exceed 2 C of global warming."]},{"k":"p","s":["So, let governments go to the next COP and explain the empty seats. Save the airfare, the emissions and two weeks of time better spent elsewhere. Instead, use a fraction of that time to ask your representatives about the tangible action they are taking to tackle climate change."]}],"chars":4492}};
